{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NaThLEcVepWVNF44W4EEYU","type":"tool_result","content":"== A04 Trustworthy attribution gap high\nREQ Assign instance and tenant identity in the trusted execution layer. Don't accept labels the model supplies. Record the delegated subject — the user or system whose authority is being used — separately from the agent's identity. Test that the agent can't pose as another instance or tenant in requests or audit records. Test that trace context survives handoffs between async jobs. Treat trace IDs and caller-supplied labels only as a way to link records. They never prove identity or permission.\nNC [{\"problem\": \"Agent sharing the launching user's identity\", \"owner\": \"A01\"}, {\"problem\": \"Prompt a parent gave a sub-agent not recorded\", \"owner\": \"A06\"}, {\"problem\": \"Sub-agent authorized using an earlier actor's authority\", \"owner\": \"E08\"}, {\"problem\": \"Action records missing any of the six identity fields\", \"owner\": \"A02\"}]\nEV [{\"file\": \"app/tools/memory.py\", \"line\": 44, \"note\": \"memory_read takes the tenant from a model-filled argument, even though other tools use the verified tenant.\"}]\nALSO ['R05'] ['red_flags_found', 'violates', 'also_affects', 'summary', 'next_step', 'lead_role']\n  A04.1 no app/tools/memory.py:44 | business_unit = args.get(\"business_unit\") or ident.tenant\n  A04.2 no app/tools/memory.py:44 | business_unit = args.get(\"business_unit\") or ident.tenant\n  A04.3 yes app/audit.py:107 | ident.delegated_subject,\n  A04.4 yes app/main.py:159 | asyncio.create_task(request.app.state.agent.run(ident, task))\n  A04.5 yes app/gate.py:51 | approval = await self.approvals.find_valid(ident, tool.name, target)\n== A05 Operational lookup gap medium\nREQ Start from one suspicious action. Find the team responsible, the current operator, the deployment manifest, and the live instance. Show that you can contain the right instance or agent type without cutting off the launching user's other access.\nNC [{\"problem\": \"Stop doesn't halt running work or open tool streams within a set time\", \"owner\": \"R11\"}, {\"problem\": \"No drill for a compromised shared tool or agent type\", \"owner\": \"E12\"}, {\"problem\": \"Action records missing any of the six identity fields\", \"owner\": \"A02\"}]\nEV []\nALSO [] ['red_flags_found', 'violates', 'also_affects', 'summary', 'next_step', 'lead_role', 'challenge']\n  A05.1 unknown  | \n  A05.2 unknown  | \n  A05.3 no app/killswitch.py:19 |   AND (scope = 'fleet' OR scope = $1)\n== B02 Least-privilege access gap medium\nREQ Limit credentials to named operations and resources, including tenant boundaries. Test that an allowed read works. Test that an out-of-scope write, an admin action, and a request for another tenant's data all fail. Limit each token to its intended audience, so other services reject it. Remove wildcard permissions and permissions inherited from people.\nNC [{\"problem\": \"A retrieval search or cache not filtered by the requesting tenant or user\", \"owner\": \"R04\"}, {\"problem\": \"Long-lived or static secrets that never expire or rotate\", \"owner\": \"B03\"}, {\"problem\": \"Revocation delay from cached or self-contained tokens\", \"owner\": \"B04\"}, {\"problem\": \"A sub-agent getting powers beyond its task, or a parent escalating through a peer\", \"owner\": \"E08\"}, {\"problem\": \"Memory readable across tenants or tasks\", \"owner\": \"R05\"}]\nEV [{\"file\": \"app/identity.py\", \"line\": 92, \"note\": \"Agent uses its projected service account token, not a user token\"}]\nALSO [] ['red_flags_found', 'violates', 'also_affects', 'summary', 'next_step', 'lead_role', 'challenge']\n  B02.1 unknown  | \n  B02.2 no app/tools/memory.py:44 | business_unit = args.get(\"business_unit\") or ident.tenant\n  B02.3 unknown  | \n  B02.4 yes app/identity.py:92 | return Path(self.settings.workload_token_path).read_text().strip()\n== B04 Independent revocation gap medium\nREQ Show that an operator can cut off this agent's access without cutting off the user who launched it. The agent must not need to cooperate. Set and measure the longest time before the cutoff takes effect. Count cached tokens, self-contained tokens, and open sessions. A trusted enforcement point must block later calls within a time limit that fits the potential harm. Revoking only the refresh token is not enough. If tokens live longer than that limit, push the revocation to each service (for example, with OpenID CAEP session-revoked events) or make the tokens shorter-lived.\nNC [{\"problem\": \"A kill switch that doesn't stop running work or open tool streams\", \"owner\": \"R11\"}, {\"problem\": \"Sub-agents or remote workers still acting after the parent is stopped\", \"owner\": \"E09\"}, {\"problem\": \"Static API keys used where short-lived credentials are available\", \"owner\": \"B03\"}, {\"problem\": \"No way to trace a suspicious action to its team, operator, and live instance\", \"owner\": \"A05\"}]\nEV []\nALSO [] ['red_flags_found', 'violates', 'also_affects', 'summary', 'next_step', 'lead_role', 'challenge']\n  B04.1 unknown  | \n  B04.2 no app/loop.py:127 | await killswitch.assert_running(pool, ident.tenant)\n  B04.3 no app/identity.py:97, deploy/k8s/deployment.yaml:107 | if cached and cached.expires_at - 30 > time.time():\nexpirationSeconds: 600\n  B04.4 no README.md:58 | `'tenant:<bu>'`, `halted = true`) as `procurement_ops`. New runs refuse to\n== C02 Review security-relevant changes gap medium\nREQ Require diffs with a named author, plus review, for changes to the manifest and its policies. Show who is allowed to change production config. Record emergency changes with an owner, a reason, an end date, and a follow-up review.\nNC [{\"problem\": \"Running config drifting from the approved baseline unnoticed\", \"owner\": \"C04\"}, {\"problem\": \"Release candidate not re-tested against attack cases\", \"owner\": \"C06\"}, {\"problem\": \"N