 a higher-authority approval\", \"owner\": \"B05\"}, {\"problem\": \"Hidden instructions inside a tool's metadata\", \"owner\": \"E04\"}, {\"problem\": \"Outbound traffic to unapproved internet destinations\", \"owner\": \"B09\"}]\nEV [{\"file\": \"deploy/k8s/deployment.yaml\", \"line\": 47, \"note\": \"ERP is reached only through the gateway URL\"}]\nALSO [] ['red_flags_found', 'violates', 'also_affects', 'summary', 'next_step', 'lead_role', 'challenge']\n  E06.1 yes deploy/k8s/deployment.yaml:47 | value: \"https://erp-mcp-gateway.erp-mcp-gateway.svc.cluster.local:8443/mcp\"\n  E06.2 unknown  | \n  E06.3 unknown  | \n  E06.4 unknown  | \n  E06.5 no app/mcp_client.py:70, app/mcp_client.py:110 | self._tools: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = {}\nself._tools = {t[\"name\"]: t for t in tools}\n  E06.6 unknown  | \n== R04 Retrieval-corpus integrity gap medium\nREQ The retrieval corpus is the set of documents the agent searches for context. Its index stores those documents, or smaller passages called chunks, in a search engine or vector database. Limit which identities and sources can add or change content there. For each chunk, keep its source, when it was added, its trust level, and its access permissions. Enforce the requesting tenant's access when searching. Test an unapproved attempt to add content and a search across tenants. Also test quarantining, expiring, and revoking access to seeded test documents. Confirm the affected chunks disappear from search results and caches within a stated time. See the [R04 recipe](CHECKLIST-VERIFICATION.md#r--run-time).\nNC [{\"problem\": \"Memory entries poisoned or shared across tenants\", \"owner\": \"R05\"}, {\"problem\": \"Agent credentials allowing another tenant's data at the API\", \"owner\": \"B02\"}, {\"problem\": \"Retrieved chunks not checked for size, type, or hidden instructions\", \"owner\": \"R01\"}, {\"problem\": \"Embedding or reranker model swapped without review\", \"owner\": \"C05\"}]\nEV [{\"file\": \"release/manifest.yaml\", \"line\": 91, \"note\": \"manifest states retrieval: none\"}, {\"file\": \"app/tools/documents.py\", \"line\": 24, \"note\": \"documents are read by doc_id within the tenant, with no search or index\"}]\nALSO [] ['red_flags_found', 'violates', 'also_affects', 'summary', 'next_step', 'lead_role', 'challenge']\n  R04.1 unknown  | \n  R04.2 no app/tools/memory.py:94 | args.get(\"source_doc_id\"),\n  R04.3 no app/tools/memory.py:44 | business_unit = args.get(\"business_unit\") or ident.tenant\n  R04.4 unknown  | \n== R05 Memory isolation and write validation gap high\nREQ Separate memory by tenant, agent type, instance, and task as needed. Block access across those lines unless it is clearly approved. Check what gets written to memory. Test that one poisoned run can't quietly plant instructions in another run's memory. Don't move the agent's own output into trusted memory without review, and let unverified entries expire. Write checks must also cover content that arrives through ordinary queries, not just special write paths.\nNC [{\"problem\": \"No record of who wrote a memory entry, or no way to remove it\", \"owner\": \"R06\"}, {\"problem\": \"Retrieval search not filtered by the requesting tenant\", \"owner\": \"R04\"}, {\"problem\": \"Agent credentials allowing another tenant's data at the API\", \"owner\": \"B02\"}, {\"problem\": \"Rollback restoring old memory or index state unchecked\", \"owner\": \"C07\"}]\nEV [{\"file\": \"app/tools/memory.py\", \"line\": 44, \"note\": \"memory_read uses a model-supplied business_unit, so one tenant's run can read another tenant's notes.\"}]\nALSO ['A04'] ['red_flags_found', 'violates', 'also_affects', 'summary', 'next_step', 'lead_role']\n  R05.1 no app/tools/memory.py:44 | business_unit = args.get(\"business_unit\") or ident.tenant\n  R05.2 yes app/tools/memory.py:73 | check_note(args[\"body\"])\n  R05.3 yes app/tools/memory.py:83 | ) VALUES ($1, $2, $3, $4, $5, false, false, now() + interval '30 days',\n  R05.4 y